WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.100 --> 00:00:03.567
-Newly unearthed texts
from the phone

00:00:03.567 --> 00:00:05.234
of Donald Trump's
former chief of staff

00:00:05.234 --> 00:00:07.033
have revealed that many
of the key plotters

00:00:07.033 --> 00:00:08.901
behind the coup attempt
on January 6th

00:00:08.901 --> 00:00:10.901
were sitting members
of Congress,

00:00:10.901 --> 00:00:12.334
some of whom called for Trump

00:00:12.334 --> 00:00:13.901
to use martial law
to stay in power.

00:00:13.901 --> 00:00:15.868
The revelations come as
the January 6 committee

00:00:15.868 --> 00:00:17.367
prepares to make
criminal referrals

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.501
to the Justice Department.

00:00:18.501 --> 00:00:20.167
Oh, and Trump teased
a major announcement

00:00:20.167 --> 00:00:21.400
that ended up being
a major dud.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:23.467
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:23.467 --> 00:00:25.534
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:27.133 --> 00:00:29.934
Trump has been bizarrely quiet
the last few weeks,

00:00:29.934 --> 00:00:32.367
which is suspicious given
he's supposedly

00:00:32.367 --> 00:00:34.300
running for president
of the United States.

00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:36.434
But then yesterday,
he posted an image of himself

00:00:36.434 --> 00:00:40.334
in a Superman style costume
with laser eyes and the text,

00:00:40.334 --> 00:00:42.000
"America needs a superhero.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:43.701
I'll be making a major
announcement tomorrow."

00:00:43.701 --> 00:00:45.200
Now, this led
to wild speculation

00:00:45.200 --> 00:00:46.601
about what he was going to do.

00:00:46.601 --> 00:00:48.400
Maybe it had something to do
with his presidential bid

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:50.834
or the mounting
legal woes he's facing.

00:00:50.834 --> 00:00:52.467
Or maybe he was about to unveil

00:00:52.467 --> 00:00:54.567
a chintzy knockoff
superhero doll

00:00:54.567 --> 00:00:57.467
your grandmother would buy
at a dollar store for Christmas.

00:00:57.467 --> 00:00:59.167
"But Grandma,
I wanted Deadpool!"

00:00:59.167 --> 00:01:01.901
"This is even better.
It's Braindeadpool."

00:01:01.901 --> 00:01:03.400
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:05.734
"The guy at the store told me
it was just as good."

00:01:05.734 --> 00:01:09.334
But when Trump finally posted
his major announcement today,

00:01:09.334 --> 00:01:12.267
it turned out to be
so much more pathetic

00:01:12.267 --> 00:01:14.934
than anyone could have
possibly imagined.

00:01:14.934 --> 00:01:18.367
♪♪

00:01:18.367 --> 00:01:20.400
Hello, everyone.
This is Donald Trump,

00:01:20.400 --> 00:01:22.934
hopefully your favorite
president of all time --

00:01:22.934 --> 00:01:25.801
better than Lincoln,
better than Washington --

00:01:25.801 --> 00:01:27.801
with an important
announcement to make.

00:01:27.801 --> 00:01:29.467
I'm doing my first official

00:01:29.467 --> 00:01:31.901
Donald J. Trump
NFT collection,

00:01:31.901 --> 00:01:33.167
right here and right now.

00:01:33.167 --> 00:01:36.501
They're called
Trump Digital Trading Cards.

00:01:36.501 --> 00:01:39.567
These cards feature some of
the really incredible artwork

00:01:39.567 --> 00:01:41.734
pertaining to my life
and my career.

00:01:41.734 --> 00:01:43.000
It's been very exciting.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:45.000
-That IS very exciting.

00:01:45.000 --> 00:01:46.501
[ Laughter ]

00:01:46.501 --> 00:01:48.567
I bet Lincoln's
super [bleep] jealous

00:01:48.567 --> 00:01:51.601
he didn't think of that.

00:01:51.601 --> 00:01:54.133
But, real quick, which part
of your life and your career

00:01:54.133 --> 00:01:55.634
is sunglass astronaut?

00:01:55.634 --> 00:01:57.634
'Cause I feel like
I would've remembered that.

00:01:57.634 --> 00:01:59.300
Also, got to love the timing

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:01.868
of a former president
launching his NFT line

00:02:01.868 --> 00:02:04.033
the same week a crypto scammer
gets arrested.

00:02:04.033 --> 00:02:05.267
[As Trump] They got SBF.

00:02:05.267 --> 00:02:07.501
Looks like there's
an opening available, then.

00:02:07.501 --> 00:02:08.734
[ Laughter ]

00:02:08.734 --> 00:02:11.067
[Normal voice] I'm also certain
Trump didn't look

00:02:11.067 --> 00:02:13.834
at the copy of his script
until the cameras were rolling,

00:02:13.834 --> 00:02:16.033
as evidenced
by this line reading.

00:02:16.033 --> 00:02:19.100
-Each card comes with
an automatic chance

00:02:19.100 --> 00:02:21.667
to win amazing prizes,
like dinner with me.

00:02:21.667 --> 00:02:23.634
I don't know if that's
an amazing prize,

00:02:23.634 --> 00:02:25.801
but it's what we have.

00:02:25.801 --> 00:02:27.968
-[As Trump]
It's what we have, you know.

00:02:27.968 --> 00:02:29.267
Is it the best prize?

00:02:29.267 --> 00:02:30.734
It's not.
But, you know, it's Christmas.

00:02:30.734 --> 00:02:34.734
And on Christmas, isn't what
we have enough, you know?

00:02:34.734 --> 00:02:36.234
Because one day
you're president,

00:02:36.234 --> 00:02:37.767
and the next day
you're selling a product

00:02:37.767 --> 00:02:39.434
you don't fully comprehend.

00:02:39.434 --> 00:02:40.767
[ Laughter ]

00:02:40.767 --> 00:02:42.901
But who needs an iPad
when you can have a...

00:02:42.901 --> 00:02:44.968
whatever the [bleep] this is?

00:02:44.968 --> 00:02:46.300
[ Laughter ]

00:02:46.300 --> 00:02:48.934
[Normal voice] And then
the ad ended with this.

00:02:48.934 --> 00:02:51.734
-Remember, Christmas is coming,

00:02:51.734 --> 00:02:55.000
and this makes
a great Christmas gift.

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:56.601
-No, it doesn't.

00:02:56.601 --> 00:02:59.734
I don't care if you're the
biggest Trump fan in the world.

00:02:59.734 --> 00:03:01.467
If, on Christmas morning,

00:03:01.467 --> 00:03:03.400
you give your spouse
a thoughtful gift

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:05.267
in a beautifully wrapped box
with the bow on it

00:03:05.267 --> 00:03:08.267
that they get to open and
physically hold in their hands,

00:03:08.267 --> 00:03:09.434
and then they turn around

00:03:09.434 --> 00:03:11.400
and tell you,
"Your gift isn't here --

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:13.234
it's a digital trading card
of Donald Trump

00:03:13.234 --> 00:03:14.467
as a sunglass astronaut,"

00:03:14.467 --> 00:03:16.067
you're getting a divorce.

00:03:16.067 --> 00:03:17.234
[ Laughter ]

00:03:17.234 --> 00:03:19.367
This proves once again
that for anyone involved

00:03:19.367 --> 00:03:21.200
in the attempted coup
on January 6th,

00:03:21.200 --> 00:03:22.534
things will not end well.

00:03:22.534 --> 00:03:24.634
In Trump's case,
he's now such a pariah,

00:03:24.634 --> 00:03:26.634
he's hawking scam
digital trading cards

00:03:26.634 --> 00:03:28.334
on a social media site
no one's heard of.

00:03:28.334 --> 00:03:31.667
Others may face jail time or
lawsuits or lose their elections

00:03:31.667 --> 00:03:33.334
or possibly their law licenses,

00:03:33.334 --> 00:03:36.033
like in the case of former
Trump attorney Rudy Giuliani.

00:03:36.033 --> 00:03:38.868
Today, a disciplinary panel
for the D.C. Bar Association

00:03:38.868 --> 00:03:41.467
found that Rudy
had broken attorney rules

00:03:41.467 --> 00:03:42.968
in trying to overturn
the election.

00:03:42.968 --> 00:03:44.133
If the entire board agrees,

00:03:44.133 --> 00:03:46.067
that means
Rudy could be disbarred.

00:03:46.067 --> 00:03:49.000
Rudy already had to sit through
a disciplinary hearing

00:03:49.000 --> 00:03:50.734
earlier this month,
which was held virtually.

00:03:50.734 --> 00:03:52.701
And at one point in the hearing,

00:03:52.701 --> 00:03:55.334
he admitted to a weird
wardrobe malfunction

00:03:55.334 --> 00:03:56.901
when he thought
the camera was off.

00:03:56.901 --> 00:03:59.167
Now, heads up --
The video quality is not great,

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:01.434
but it's still
definitely worth watching.

00:04:06.667 --> 00:04:08.334
[ Speaking indistinctly ]

00:04:12.767 --> 00:04:13.934
That's right.

00:04:13.934 --> 00:04:16.200
For some reason,
Rudy accidentally had

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:19.367
two watches on the same wrist...

00:04:19.367 --> 00:04:21.033
[ Laughter ]

00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.934
...and didn't realize it
until he was already

00:04:22.934 --> 00:04:24.334
in the middle
of a disciplinary hearing

00:04:24.334 --> 00:04:25.834
to review his law license.

00:04:25.834 --> 00:04:27.033
[As Giuliani] Done so soon?

00:04:27.033 --> 00:04:28.067
But it's only two.

00:04:28.067 --> 00:04:31.067
Oh, but two twice,
so that's four.

00:04:31.067 --> 00:04:33.000
[Normal voice] Two watches feels
like one of those things

00:04:33.000 --> 00:04:34.467
that would cause
your grandchildren

00:04:34.467 --> 00:04:36.701
to sit you at the kitchen table
and start showing you brochures.

00:04:36.701 --> 00:04:39.033
"What about this place, Pepaw?

00:04:39.033 --> 00:04:41.367
Look, it has a pond with ducks.
You like ducks."

00:04:41.367 --> 00:04:43.934
Anyway, I feel like that
can't exactly help your case

00:04:43.934 --> 00:04:45.534
when you're trying
to keep your law license.

00:04:45.534 --> 00:04:47.701
"Mr. Giuliani, do you feel
you're capable of performing

00:04:47.701 --> 00:04:49.200
the duties as a lawyer?"
"I do."

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.868
"Okay, and are you aware
that you have a pair of pants on

00:04:51.868 --> 00:04:53.200
where your shirt should be,
and a shirt

00:04:53.200 --> 00:04:55.968
where your pants should be?"
"I was not, but, uh...

00:04:55.968 --> 00:04:58.467
that would explain why
I keep poking myself in the eye

00:04:58.467 --> 00:05:01.400
whenever I try
to scratch my butt."

00:05:01.400 --> 00:05:03.501
I can't even wrap my head
around the logistics of this.

00:05:03.501 --> 00:05:05.501
I could maybe see putting
a watch on each wrist.

00:05:05.501 --> 00:05:07.767
But how do you put
a second watch on your wrist

00:05:07.767 --> 00:05:10.400
without noticing the first one
that's already there?

00:05:10.400 --> 00:05:12.000
I mean, maybe he's just trying

00:05:12.000 --> 00:05:13.667
to get a new mobster name
to catch on.

00:05:13.667 --> 00:05:14.767
[As Giuliani]
Check it out, fellas.

00:05:14.767 --> 00:05:16.434
I guess you can call me
Rudy Two Watches.

00:05:16.434 --> 00:05:17.701
[Normal voice] Nah.

00:05:17.701 --> 00:05:20.901
We're just gonna keep
calling you Dumb Rudy.

00:05:20.901 --> 00:05:22.133
[As Giuliani]
Hey, you better watch it.

00:05:22.133 --> 00:05:23.634
You better watch it.
[ Beeping ]

00:05:23.634 --> 00:05:25.634
Oh, hold on. That's my alarm.

00:05:25.634 --> 00:05:27.834
[ Beeping ]
Oh, and that's my second alarm

00:05:27.834 --> 00:05:30.334
that's telling me
to turn my first alarm off.

00:05:30.334 --> 00:05:32.334
[Normal voice]
So, Rudy is already...

00:05:32.334 --> 00:05:34.701
[ Laughter ]

00:05:34.701 --> 00:05:36.467
Rudy is already
facing consequences.

00:05:36.467 --> 00:05:38.033
Meanwhile, the committee
investigating

00:05:38.033 --> 00:05:39.367
the January 6th insurrection
has announced

00:05:39.367 --> 00:05:41.868
that it will hold its final
public meeting next week

00:05:41.868 --> 00:05:44.334
before releasing a full report
on the coup attempt

00:05:44.334 --> 00:05:46.767
and making criminal referrals
to the Justice Department.

00:05:46.767 --> 00:05:49.067
While it's unclear which names
will be on that list,

00:05:49.067 --> 00:05:51.601
there are some that seem
more obvious than others.

00:05:51.601 --> 00:05:54.467
-What may be the last acts
of the January 6th

00:05:54.467 --> 00:05:56.968
Select House Committee.
Chairman Bennie Thompson

00:05:56.968 --> 00:05:59.467
says the panel will hold
its final public meeting

00:05:59.467 --> 00:06:00.868
next Monday,

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:03.167
where its final report
is expected to be approved.

00:06:03.167 --> 00:06:05.400
The chairman says announcements
about criminal referrals

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.400
will be made on Monday.

00:06:07.400 --> 00:06:08.968
-We're expecting the names
of the folks

00:06:08.968 --> 00:06:11.701
who would be referred for
potential criminal prosecution

00:06:11.701 --> 00:06:14.334
to the Justice Department,
as well as the rationale

00:06:14.334 --> 00:06:16.267
for why they are being referred.

00:06:16.267 --> 00:06:18.400
-Now, former President Trump
is expected to be

00:06:18.400 --> 00:06:21.100
at the top of the list
for criminal referral.

00:06:21.100 --> 00:06:22.634
-That's right.
Donald Trump is high on the list

00:06:22.634 --> 00:06:24.300
of potential names
for criminal referrals.

00:06:24.300 --> 00:06:26.067
Now, I don't know
if his name will be on there,

00:06:26.067 --> 00:06:28.067
but if it's not, that would be
quite the letdown.

00:06:28.067 --> 00:06:30.734
It'd be like if the finale
of "White Lotus" never ended up

00:06:30.734 --> 00:06:32.133
getting around
to telling you who died,

00:06:32.133 --> 00:06:34.968
the whole episode was just
Jennifer Coolidge going,

00:06:34.968 --> 00:06:37.300
"Ohh, wow."

00:06:37.300 --> 00:06:38.801
[ Laughter ]

00:06:38.801 --> 00:06:41.133
"Wowwwww."

00:06:41.133 --> 00:06:43.300
Which would honestly be great.

00:06:43.300 --> 00:06:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:06:44.667 --> 00:06:47.067
This committee has been in
existence for a year and a half.

00:06:47.067 --> 00:06:49.467
How could they not have
enough evidence at this point

00:06:49.467 --> 00:06:50.801
for a criminal referral
for the guy

00:06:50.801 --> 00:06:52.467
who incited the insurrection
in the first place?

00:06:52.467 --> 00:06:53.968
Like, can you imagine
the committee

00:06:53.968 --> 00:06:55.501
gaveling to a close
for the final time?

00:06:55.501 --> 00:06:58.067
"Well, we've spent 17 months
painstakingly reconstructing

00:06:58.067 --> 00:06:59.734
a minute-by-minute timeline
of the events that day.

00:06:59.734 --> 00:07:01.501
We've tracked down Trump's
every movement.

00:07:01.501 --> 00:07:03.100
We've documented
every communication he made.

00:07:03.100 --> 00:07:04.367
We've corroborated
every connection

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:05.767
he had to the central figures

00:07:05.767 --> 00:07:07.400
involved in fomenting
the deadliest attack

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:09.133
on American democracy
since the Civil War.

00:07:09.133 --> 00:07:11.534
And we're just [bleep]
stumped, dudes."

00:07:11.534 --> 00:07:13.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:13.701 --> 00:07:16.033
"Ohh, wow."

00:07:16.033 --> 00:07:18.567
[ Laughter ]

00:07:18.567 --> 00:07:20.000
Congressman Jamie Raskin,

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:21.334
who is one of
the committee members

00:07:21.334 --> 00:07:23.367
making decisions about possible
criminal referrals,

00:07:23.367 --> 00:07:25.734
told Politico that all of
the members involved

00:07:25.734 --> 00:07:28.100
have legal experience and are
looking at the case as lawyers.

00:07:37.434 --> 00:07:38.767
Okay, but I'm guessing

00:07:38.767 --> 00:07:40.934
law school final exams
aren't this easy.

00:07:40.934 --> 00:07:43.601
This is like a $200
"Jeopardy!" answer

00:07:43.601 --> 00:07:46.200
in a category called
Rhymes With Reason.

00:07:46.200 --> 00:07:47.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.701 --> 00:07:50.701
Although maybe,
maybe they are that easy.

00:07:50.701 --> 00:07:53.334
I mean, Rudy's a lawyer,
so it can't be too hard.

00:07:53.334 --> 00:07:55.467
[As Giuliani] Good news, boss.
I passed the law school exam.

00:07:55.467 --> 00:07:57.968
It was on the back
of a cereal box.

00:07:57.968 --> 00:08:00.200
There was a watch inside,
but I already had one.

00:08:00.200 --> 00:08:01.701
So now I wear both.

00:08:01.701 --> 00:08:03.033
You know, like a normal guy.

00:08:03.033 --> 00:08:04.801
That's why they call me

00:08:04.801 --> 00:08:06.300
Dumb Rudy.

00:08:06.300 --> 00:08:08.067
[ Laughter ]

00:08:08.067 --> 00:08:09.601
[Normal voice] The more
suspenseful question is,

00:08:09.601 --> 00:08:11.701
who else will get
a criminal referral?

00:08:11.701 --> 00:08:13.534
Because as we've learned
this week,

00:08:13.534 --> 00:08:15.868
the committee is in possession
of secret text messages

00:08:15.868 --> 00:08:18.234
from the phone of former Trump
chief of staff Mark Meadows,

00:08:18.234 --> 00:08:21.901
and those text messages reveal
that many of the key organizers

00:08:21.901 --> 00:08:23.400
of the attempt
to overthrow the election

00:08:23.400 --> 00:08:25.501
were sitting members
of Congress.

00:08:25.501 --> 00:08:28.467
-Nearly two years after
the January 6th insurrection,

00:08:28.467 --> 00:08:31.634
thousands of previously unseen
text messages

00:08:31.634 --> 00:08:34.667
are revealing the lengths
to which Republican lawmakers

00:08:34.667 --> 00:08:37.767
went in their efforts
to overturn the 2020 election.

00:08:37.767 --> 00:08:39.234
They show Meadows
in conversation

00:08:39.234 --> 00:08:42.133
with at least 34 Republican
members of Congress.

00:08:42.133 --> 00:08:44.467
-The trove of coup evidence from
powerful members of Congress

00:08:44.467 --> 00:08:45.701
is in writing.

00:08:45.701 --> 00:08:47.567
We made this to make sure
you understand

00:08:47.567 --> 00:08:49.901
these are the people
who were texting Meadows.

00:08:49.901 --> 00:08:51.667
Some of them --
They're not all the same.

00:08:51.667 --> 00:08:55.267
Some of them were asking
questions, lobbing in ideas,

00:08:55.267 --> 00:08:58.267
claiming that they were kind of
being an intermediary.

00:08:58.267 --> 00:09:01.534
Others -- many of them,
and we have the receipts --

00:09:01.534 --> 00:09:03.501
were actively cheering on,

00:09:03.501 --> 00:09:06.434
demanding, or supporting
an illegal coup.

00:09:06.434 --> 00:09:08.267
-So, 34 Republican members
of Congress

00:09:08.267 --> 00:09:10.334
were texting Trump's chief
of staff to help plan a coup.

00:09:10.334 --> 00:09:12.000
Did none of them think
they'd get caught?

00:09:12.000 --> 00:09:14.634
I don't text anyone that freely
unless it's my weed dealer who,

00:09:14.634 --> 00:09:17.934
for some reason I trust with my
name, address and phone number,

00:09:17.934 --> 00:09:19.434
and to whom I feel
perfectly comfortable

00:09:19.434 --> 00:09:20.434
texting things like...

00:09:21.901 --> 00:09:24.167
And then he feels
perfectly free to text back...

00:09:29.133 --> 00:09:30.467
[ Laughter ]

00:09:30.467 --> 00:09:32.734
And the texts are,
as you'd suspect, very damning.

00:09:32.734 --> 00:09:34.234
You may remember
that Georgia congresswoman

00:09:34.234 --> 00:09:36.300
Marjorie Taylor Greene,
was caught texting Meadows

00:09:36.300 --> 00:09:37.667
about the possibility of Trump

00:09:37.667 --> 00:09:39.300
declaring martial law
to stay in power

00:09:39.300 --> 00:09:40.701
and misspelling
the word "martial."

00:09:40.701 --> 00:09:43.334
Well, now we have evidence
that a second House Republican

00:09:43.334 --> 00:09:46.434
was also urging Meadows via text
to declare martial law.

00:09:46.434 --> 00:09:48.701
-Here is a text message
that was sent

00:09:48.701 --> 00:09:52.100
to Donald Trump's White House
chief of staff, Mark Meadows.

00:09:52.100 --> 00:09:55.167
It says, quote, "Mark,
in seeing what's happening

00:09:55.167 --> 00:09:58.100
so quickly and reading
about the Dominion lawsuits

00:09:58.100 --> 00:10:01.601
attempting to stop
any meaningful investigation,

00:10:01.601 --> 00:10:04.801
we are at a point of no return
in saving our republic."

00:10:04.801 --> 00:10:06.801
Exclamation point,
exclamation point.

00:10:06.801 --> 00:10:08.200
"Our" -- all caps --

00:10:08.200 --> 00:10:13.033
"...last hope is invoking
Marshall law.

00:10:13.033 --> 00:10:15.667
Please urge to president
to do so."

00:10:15.667 --> 00:10:17.934
This text message
was from a sitting member

00:10:17.934 --> 00:10:19.767
of the United States Congress --

00:10:19.767 --> 00:10:23.901
Republican Congressman
Ralph Norman of South Carolina.

00:10:23.901 --> 00:10:26.734
-This is now the second sitting
Republican member of Congress

00:10:26.734 --> 00:10:29.067
to text Trump's chief
of staff about martial law

00:10:29.067 --> 00:10:31.234
and also to misspell
the word "martial."

00:10:31.234 --> 00:10:32.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:32.667 --> 00:10:34.701
When you spell it like that,
it sounds like an old Western

00:10:34.701 --> 00:10:36.601
your grandfather keeps
telling you to watch.

00:10:36.601 --> 00:10:38.000
"You'll love it.
It's in black and white

00:10:38.000 --> 00:10:39.467
and there's no women in it.

00:10:39.467 --> 00:10:42.000
Now, does your TV
get Westinghouse?"

00:10:42.000 --> 00:10:44.667
[ Laughter ]

00:10:44.667 --> 00:10:46.934
If nothing else, watching these
people debase themselves

00:10:46.934 --> 00:10:48.868
is yet another reminder
you cannot slink away

00:10:48.868 --> 00:10:50.901
from Trump's movement
with your dignity intact.

00:10:50.901 --> 00:10:53.534
Whether it's embarrassing
texts, scam NFTs,

00:10:53.534 --> 00:10:55.267
or accidentally
wearing two watches.

00:10:55.267 --> 00:10:57.934
If you serve Donald Trump
or try to help him

00:10:57.934 --> 00:11:00.834
overthrow the government,
you will end up humiliated.

00:11:00.834 --> 00:11:02.300
It may not be as satisfying

00:11:02.300 --> 00:11:05.234
as seeing all of his accomplices
go to jail...

00:11:05.234 --> 00:11:06.567
-But it's what we have.

00:11:06.567 --> 00:11:09.567
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:11:09.567 --> 00:11:12.634
[ Cheers and applause ]

